            <ArticleTitle>All that is old does not wither: Conservation of outer kinetochore proteins across all eukaryotes?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-293</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1083/jcb.201701025</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The kinetochore drives faithful chromosome segregation in all eukaryotes, yet the underlying machinery is diverse across species. D'Archivio and Wickstead (2017. J. Cell Biol. https://doi.org/10.1083/jcb.201608043) apply sensitive homology predictions to identify proteins in kinetoplastids with similarity to canonical outer kinetochore proteins, suggesting some degree of universality in the eukaryotic kinetochore.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 Senaratne and Drinnenberg.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
